Nobody said that dunce caps can't be cursed. However, they are created
cursed, uncursed and blessed with the same percentages as cornuthaums.
Therefore, when you find an unidentified conical hat, you do not know
which it is regardless of whether it is cursed. Moreover, even if dunce
caps _were_ generated mostly cursed, if you found an uncursed conical
hat, it could still be a dunce cap, though the odds would be lower.

Therefore, if you find a conical hat, and it is not cursed (it doesn't
even matter how you found that out, by pet or otherwise), it can be
either a cornuthaum _or_ a dunce cap. If it is a dunce cap, putting it
on will make it curse itself there and then. Therefore, trying on
otherwise unidentified conical hats is unsafe _even_ if you know that it
is uncursed or even blessed.

